WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.819 --> 00:00:01.994
Hey Conan 360 Live,

00:00:01.994 --> 00:00:03.151
this is John Karounos

00:00:03.151 --> 00:00:04.971
from Warner Bros. Studio Tour Hollywood.

00:00:04.971 --> 00:00:07.087
I'm currently inside of
the picture car vault

00:00:07.087 --> 00:00:08.199
or as I like to call it

00:00:08.199 --> 00:00:09.032
The Bat Cave.

00:00:09.032 --> 00:00:11.729
I'm gonna show you around
some of my absolute

00:00:11.729 --> 00:00:12.796
favorite things.

00:00:12.796 --> 00:00:14.480
Follow me over to this Batmobile here.

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:16.982
Now, what you see is the
Batmobile from Batman Forever.

00:00:16.982 --> 00:00:20.146
That's where Val Kilmer
played Bruce Wayne and Batman.

00:00:20.146 --> 00:00:23.641
Crazy fact, the radio
in here is stuck forever

00:00:23.641 --> 00:00:24.894
on Seal's Kiss From A Rose.

00:00:24.894 --> 00:00:27.651
It's the only thing that
plays inside of the car.

00:00:27.651 --> 00:00:30.170
We also have the bikes
from Batman and Robin.

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:31.408
We have Robin's Redbird,

00:00:31.408 --> 00:00:33.917
We have Batgirl's Batblade.

00:00:33.917 --> 00:00:35.449
We also have the original,

00:00:35.449 --> 00:00:39.168
the number one hero car from Batman, 1989,

00:00:39.168 --> 00:00:41.022
Michael Keaton's car.

00:00:41.022 --> 00:00:41.882
Now, that's of course the one

00:00:41.882 --> 00:00:44.377
that Tim Burton originally directed

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:46.627
and from the Nolan Trilogy,

00:00:47.872 --> 00:00:49.002
the Bat statue.

00:00:49.002 --> 00:00:50.972
It's probably kinda hard
to see the entire thing

00:00:50.972 --> 00:00:53.178
but he's got no pants on.

00:00:53.178 --> 00:00:55.834
Who would make a statue like that?

00:00:55.834 --> 00:00:58.587
Now, clearly some of the
absolute most imposing things

00:00:58.587 --> 00:00:59.830
in this exhibit,

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:00.874
look behind you,

00:01:00.874 --> 00:01:03.245
the tumblers from The Dark Knight Trilogy.

00:01:03.245 --> 00:01:04.392
Now, this is where Christopher Nolan

00:01:04.392 --> 00:01:05.859
took over directing.

00:01:05.859 --> 00:01:08.808
And you can really see the
realistic aspect of Batman.

00:01:08.808 --> 00:01:10.047
These are the real deal.

00:01:10.047 --> 00:01:12.298
They really run and
they are the originals.

00:01:12.298 --> 00:01:15.449
They have Chevy 350, small
block V8 engines in there.

00:01:15.449 --> 00:01:17.633
So, Bruce Wayne while, you know,

00:01:17.633 --> 00:01:19.543
he is a really philanthropic guy

00:01:19.543 --> 00:01:21.651
apparently the environment,

00:01:21.651 --> 00:01:23.048
in terms of gas mileage,

00:01:23.048 --> 00:01:24.866
not on his list of priorities

00:01:24.866 --> 00:01:25.999
and that's fine.

00:01:25.999 --> 00:01:28.029
Now, you see the camouflage tumbler

00:01:28.029 --> 00:01:31.181
really make it's appearance
in The Dark Knight Rises

00:01:31.181 --> 00:01:33.353
but the black tumbler really
carries it's way through

00:01:33.353 --> 00:01:35.877
Batman Begins and The Dark Knight.

00:01:35.877 --> 00:01:39.632
But behind me we're
gonna take a closer look

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:41.881
at The Joker Car.

00:01:41.881 --> 00:01:42.852
Here we are,

00:01:42.852 --> 00:01:44.995
inside of The Joker's car.

00:01:44.995 --> 00:01:45.850
What an experience.

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:46.845
Look at this thing!

00:01:46.845 --> 00:01:48.582
We've got valor all over the roof,

00:01:48.582 --> 00:01:50.256
it's on the panels.

00:01:50.256 --> 00:01:51.934
It's like blinged out to the max.

00:01:51.934 --> 00:01:52.989
There's gold everywhere.

00:01:52.989 --> 00:01:54.141
Gold shifter.

00:01:54.141 --> 00:01:55.357
I don't know if you can see down there

00:01:55.357 --> 00:01:57.523
but there are custom Joker mats.

00:01:57.523 --> 00:01:59.043
There's like snake skin everywhere.

00:01:59.043 --> 00:02:02.998
This thing has to be a
monster to actually clean.

00:02:02.998 --> 00:02:04.836
But look at this diamond
encrusted steering wheel,

00:02:04.836 --> 00:02:06.512
surprisingly good for grip.

00:02:06.512 --> 00:02:08.116
I can see why he has that.

00:02:08.116 --> 00:02:08.949
It's amazing.

00:02:08.949 --> 00:02:11.508
And you know, reinforced roof.

00:02:11.508 --> 00:02:12.460
Because at some point,

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:13.712
it's bound to happen,

00:02:13.712 --> 00:02:15.045
somebody dressed up as a bat

00:02:15.045 --> 00:02:16.477
is going to land right on the roof,

00:02:16.477 --> 00:02:17.983
punch a hole through the thing,

00:02:17.983 --> 00:02:20.130
rip The Joker out.

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:21.806
Tight quarters, too.

00:02:21.806 --> 00:02:24.382
I can see he gets really
nuzzled up to Harley Quinn.

00:02:24.382 --> 00:02:27.568
It makes it really easy for a
romantic date night, you know.

00:02:27.568 --> 00:02:30.873
Man, I gotta get me one of these.

00:02:30.873 --> 00:02:31.989
That's gonna do it for me.

00:02:31.989 --> 00:02:33.170
Again, everybody,

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:35.718
thank you for checking out
some of my favorite things

00:02:35.718 --> 00:02:37.996
but we encourage you to
come see for yourself.

00:02:37.996 --> 00:02:42.163
So, join us, book your
tickets at wbstudiotour.com.

00:02:42.288 --> 00:02:43.882
What else can I say about this exhibit,

00:02:43.882 --> 00:02:45.467
besides the fact that it's the

00:02:45.467 --> 00:02:47.217
Bane of my existence.

00:02:48.052 --> 00:02:51.007
Don't just bring your nuclear family

00:02:51.007 --> 00:02:53.240
because this place is

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:54.073
the bomb.

00:02:55.342 --> 00:02:56.592
I am so sorry.

